                <pb facs="0291" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg187"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 25,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 542.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 1113 of the 5th
                    ultimo, relative to the claim of the American citizen Louis McCaslin against
                    China for injuries caused by the wrongful closing of a bridge of boats at
                    Ningpo, April 29, 1888. Your note in the case of the 5th ultimo is approved.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
